# The Rust staticlib is not instrumented and holds allocations alive until the
# process exits -- the tokio runtime, the datastore, lazily-built statics. None
# of that is a leak this suite can act on, and reporting it would bury the
# frames that matter.
#
# Anything allocated on the C++ side still reports: these match by the name of
# the frame that allocated, not by where the pointer ended up.
leak:surrealdb
leak:tokio
leak:std::rt
leak:rust_
